  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Stop 1",
      "h2": "The signal network",
      "body_html": "<p class=\"big\">The <span class=\"hl p\">nervous system</span> is your body's wiring.</p><p>It carries signals at up to <b>120 m/s</b> — faster than a Formula 1 car. 🏎️</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 2",
      "h2": "CNS and beyond",
      "body_html": "<p><span class=\"hl p\">CNS</span> = brain + spinal cord.</p><p><b>Peripheral</b> nerves run to every limb.</p><p>They carry messages both ways — in (sensing) and out (moving).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Stop 3",
      "h2": "Reflexes",
      "body_html": "<p>Touch a hot pan → your hand snaps back <em>before</em> you even think.</p><p>That's a <span class=\"hl y\">reflex</span>: a <b>stimulus</b> (hot) goes to the spinal cord and the <b>response</b> (pull away) returns — bypassing the brain. ⚡</p>"
    }
  ],
